00:00:03.560 --> 00:00:06.000
What did the 2010's add up to?

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:10.520
I spent the decade at Reason creating videos about the democratization of everything

00:00:10.520 --> 00:00:13.800
and the declining power of society's gatekeepers.

00:00:13.800 --> 00:00:19.020
Media theorist Marshall McLuhan, who coined the axiom, the medium is the message,

00:00:19.020 --> 00:00:23.300
argued that history's prime mover isn't the great leader or great thinker,

00:00:23.300 --> 00:00:26.300
but ever-changing communications technologies.

00:00:26.300 --> 00:00:32.520
Everything that we prize in our Western world in matters of individualism, separatism,

00:00:32.520 --> 00:00:39.500
a unique point of view, a private judgement, all those factors are highly favored by the printed word,

00:00:39.500 --> 00:00:42.600
and not really favored by other forms.

00:00:42.600 --> 00:00:47.720
As societies moved from oral traditions to written ones McLuhan argued

00:00:47.720 --> 00:00:53.600
there was a cultural shift. Tribal groups who relied on face-to-face communication and mythology

00:00:53.600 --> 00:00:57.380
morphed into more complex, less homogeneous societies.

00:00:57.380 --> 00:01:01.840
Thanks to the written word and when the printing press standardized communications,

00:01:01.840 --> 00:01:06.040
the distribution of literature created the very concept of a public,

00:01:06.040 --> 00:01:11.840
bound together by common languages and texts. This set the stage for the rise of modern nation-states

00:01:11.840 --> 00:01:16.480
and the Enlightenment. Millions of words across thousands of miles.

00:01:16.480 --> 00:01:21.240
In the 1960s McLuhan identified our current epoch as the Electric Age

00:01:21.240 --> 00:01:25.660
in which circuit based media gave rise to what he termed, the global village.

00:01:25.660 --> 00:01:30.040
For the first time in history the entire world could follow a single event.

00:01:30.040 --> 00:01:35.320
McLuhan predicted that this electric global village would undo both the national homogeneity

00:01:35.320 --> 00:01:40.960
and personal individuality engendered by print, reviving our more fractured and tribal past.

00:01:40.960 --> 00:01:45.100
We're re-tribalizing. Involuntarily we're getting rid of individualism.

00:01:45.100 --> 00:01:49.020
We're more concerned with what the group knows, with feeling as it does, of acting with it.

00:01:49.020 --> 00:01:54.600
And as the electric age has evolved into the digital age with its cheap limitless replicability,

00:01:54.600 --> 00:01:58.440
this re-tribalization has accelerated in the 2010's,

00:01:58.440 --> 00:02:01.900
which is why the past decade has both created opportunities and dangers

00:02:01.900 --> 00:02:04.740
for the libertarian and liberal worldviews.

